OL,3,GNEWSABrothers battled wild weather in
OL,4,ALoch Ness race
OL,5,
OL,6,FTwo brothers have described how they
OL,7,Fbattled "chaotic weather" to row across
OL,8,FLoch Ness as part of a challenge.
OL,10,FJoshua Le Lere, 29, and Adam Le Lere,
OL,11,F24, from Jersey, finished third in the
OL,12,FMonster the Loch challenge in Scotland
OL,13,Flast month.
OL,15,FThey rowed the full 22.7 miles (36.5km)
OL,16,Fof Loch Ness in 58 minutes and 13
OL,17,Fseconds.
OL,19,FAs they confronted "all four seasons in
OL,20,Fa day", Joshua said: "We just held on.
OL,21,FWe just kept going, kept pushing."
